==Genetics==
Unlike some other species in [[Rosa sect. Caninae|''Rosa'' sect. ''Caninae'']] which are pentaploid with an unusual [[meiosis]] referred to as [[Rosa canina#Genetics|permanent odd polyploidy]], ''R.&nbsp;micrantha'' has been found to be hexaploid with fully sexual reproduction.<ref>{{citation |title=Microsatellite Analyses of Artificial and Spontaneous Dogrose Hybrids Reveal the Hybridogenic Origin of ''Rosa micrantha'' by the Contribution of Unreduced Gametes |author=Christiane Mritz and Volker Wissemann |year=2011 |doi=10.1093/jhered/esq124}}</ref>

